      en: "Slievemore (Irish: Sliabh Mór) is a mountain on Achill Island, County Mayo, the highest point at 672 m. It is composed of quartzite and schist. The slopes contain the ruins of prehistoric villages. The name means 'big mountain'. It is part of the Achill Head Geopark. The terrain is rugged, with blanket bogs and heath, offering panoramic views of the Atlantic.",
